<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Act of Settlement 1662</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1662</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/act-of-settlement-1701">Act of Settlement</a> 1662 was a law of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parliament-of-ireland">Irish Parliament</a> that set out the terms for redistributing land in Ireland after the Restoration of Charles II. It largely confirmed Cromwellian soldiers and adventurers in the lands confiscated from Catholics after the rising of 1641, while allowing some Catholics judged 'innocent' to recover estates. The Act of Explanation of 1665 modified it, and Catholic landholding remained greatly reduced.</p></div>
